<title>FRANCE: EU grants free-market grain exports.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-market grain exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free-market grain to non-EU countries, European grain industry sources said.</p>
<p>		     Tonnage		    Maximum Rebate</p>
<p> Soft wheat	398,500		    12.90 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p> Barley	    145,700		    27.49 Ecus/tonne</p>
<p>There was no immediate official confirmation of the awards and grain sources said they were still awaiting news on possible other grain sales, expected to be of oats.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
